ía","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":2},{"y":1065,"t":"gain","x":"1065: Murcia is independent again.","cp":"taifa-of-valencia","cpn":"Taifa of Valencia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":2},{"y":1078,"t":"loss","x":"1078: Seville takes Murcia.","cp":"taifa-of-seville","cpn":"Taifa of Seville","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":3},{"y":1145,"t":"gain","x":"1145: Murcia is independent again under Abd Allah ibn Iyad.","cp":"almoravid-dynasty","cpn":"Almoravid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":2},{"y":1147,"t":"rename","x":"1147: Ibn Mardanish takes Murcia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Sa'd_ibn_Mardanish","c":2},{"y":1147,"t":"gain","x":"1147 (August): Valencia passes to Ibn Mardanish.","m":8,"cp":"taifa-of-valencia","cpn":"Taifa of Valencia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Valencia","c":2},{"y":1149,"t":"gain","x":"1149 (June, latest): Dénia is in Ibn Mardanish's hands.","m":6,"cp":"almoravid-dynasty","cpn":"Almoravid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Sa'd_ibn_Mardanish","c":1},{"y":1152,"t":"gain","x":"1152: Cliopatria's outline jumps from 9,404 to 77,869 km2.","cp":"almoravid-dynasty","cpn":"Almoravid dynasty","u":"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Mardanis","c":1},{"y":1165,"t":"contest_start","x":"1165: the Almohads march on Lorca.","cp":"almohad-caliphate","cpn":"Almohad Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Sa'd_ibn_Mardanish","c":3},{"y":1168,"t":"loss","x":"1168 (latest): Albarracín leaves Ibn Mardanish.","cp":"Pedro Ruiz de Azagra","u":"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Mardanis","c":2},{"y":1169,"t":"loss","x":"1169: the north-east of the outline is withdrawn.","cp":"crown-of-aragon","cpn":"Crown of Aragon","u":"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Mardanis","c":1},{"y":1172,"t":"contest_end","x":"1172: the fighting over the Murcian frontier ends with the Almohad takeover (see the loss event).","cp":"almohad-caliphate","cpn":"Almohad Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":2},{"y":1172,"t":"loss","x":"1172: the Almohads take Murcia.","cp":"almohad-caliphate","cpn":"Almohad Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":2},{"y":1228,"t":"gain","x":"1228: most of al-Andalus, except Valencia, passes to Ibn Hud.","cp":"almohad-caliphate","cpn":"Almohad Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":2},{"y":1228,"t":"rename","x":"1228: the Banu Hud rule Murcia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":3},{"y":1228,"t":"gain","x":"1228 (May): Ibn Hud takes Murcia.","m":5,"cp":"almohad-caliphate","cpn":"Almohad Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":3},{"y":1231,"t":"contest_start","x":"1231: Castile defeats Ibn Hud.","cp":"kingdom-of-castile","cpn":"Kingdom of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":3},{"y":1232,"t":"loss","x":"1232: Ibn Nasr rises at Jaén.","cp":"emirate-of-granada","cpn":"Emirate of Granada","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":2},{"y":1234,"t":"loss","x":"1234: Niebla leaves Ibn Hud's realm.","cp":"taifa-of-niebla","cpn":"Taifa of Niebla","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa","c":2},{"y":1235,"t":"contest_end","x":"1235: the Jerez contest with the Kingdom of Castile is closed in the last year of that state's dossier.","cp":"kingdom-of-castile","cpn":"Kingdom of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":1},{"y":1236,"t":"loss","x":"1236: Córdoba falls to Castile.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":2},{"y":1237,"t":"loss","x":"1237: Granada goes to Ibn Nasr.","m":5,"cp":"emirate-of-granada","cpn":"Emirate of Granada","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","c":2},{"y":1238,"t":"loss","x":"1238: Almería passes to Ibn Nasr.","cp":"emirate-of-granada","cpn":"Emirate of Granada","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almer%C3%ADa","c":2},{"y":1238,"t":"loss","x":"1238 (after Ibn Hud's assassination in January): Seville and the south-west leave the Murcian realm.","cp":"Banu al-Bajji","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_I_of_Granada","c":1},{"y":1239,"t":"loss","x":"1239: Málaga passes to Ibn Nasr.","cp":"emirate-of-granada","cpn":"Emirate of Granada","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_I_of_Granada","c":2},{"y":1243,"t":"rename","x":"1243: Murcia swears fealty to Castile (April, Treaty of Alcaraz).","m":4,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alcaraz","c":3},{"y":1244,"t":"loss","x":"1244: Castile conquers Lorca and Mula.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alcaraz","c":3},{"y":1245,"t":"loss","x":"1245: Cartagena falls to Alfonso.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alcaraz","c":3},{"y":1266,"t":"dissolve","x":"1266: Murcia is absorbed by Castile.","cp":"crown-of-castile","cpn":"Crown of Castile","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Battle of Fahs al-Jullab","from":1165,"to":1172,"outcome":"Almohad victory: Ibn Mardanish's army was routed in the Guadalentín valley in September-October 1165 and Murcia fell to the Almohads in 1172.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Sa'd_ibn_Mardanish"},{"name":"Ibn Hud's rebellion against the Almohads","from":1228,"to":1238,"outcome":"Ibn Hud overthrew the Almohad governors from May 1228 and took most of al-Andalus except Valencia (Zayyan ibn Mardanish); Castile (Jerez 1231, Córdoba 1236) and Ibn Nasr (Jaén 1232, Granada May 1237, Almería 1238, Málaga 1239) took it back; Ibn Hud was…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud"},{"name":"Castilian campaigns against Ibn Hud","from":1231,"to":1236,"outcome":"Castile defeated Ibn Hud at Jerez in 1231 and took Córdoba in 1236.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud"},{"name":"Conquest of Murcia in 1243","from":1243,"to":1245,"outcome":"Murcia accepted Castilian vassalage at Alcaraz in April 1243 and garrisons in its fortresses; Lorca and Mula fell in 1244 and Cartagena in spring 1245.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alcaraz"},{"name":"Mudéjar revolt of 1264-1266","from":1264,"to":1266,"outcome":"The revolt 'effectively nullified' Alfonso X's obligations under the Treaty of Alcaraz; Murcia was absorbed by Castile in 1266 after the Aragonese conquest of 1265-1266.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alcaraz"}],"certainty":[{"from":1011,"to":1266,"level":"soft","note":"Every frontier is approximate: the pages name towns and provinces (Murcia, Valencia, Dénia, Lorca, Mula, Cartagena, Jaén, Granada, Almería), not boundaries."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","title":"Taifa of Murcia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Sa'd_ibn_Mardanish","title":"Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Mardanish"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alcaraz","title":"Treaty of Alcaraz"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibn_Hud","title":"Ibn Hud"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almohad_Caliphate","title":"Almohad Caliphate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Valencia","title":"Taifa of Valencia"},{"url":"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Mardanis","title":"Muhammad ibn Mardanis (Spanish Wikipedia)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_I_of_Granada","title":"Muhammad I of Granada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almer%C3%ADa","title":"Almería"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa","title":"Taifa"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Seville","title":"History of Seville"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Seville","title":"Siege of Seville"}]}